1
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:17,200
Yongmei,

2
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:18,720
how have you been?

3
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:23,890
I've been really swamped
with work this week.

4
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,080
I'm sorry

5
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,330
for being late again today.

6
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:32,080
Don't be mad at me.

7
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:54,759
Yongmei,

8
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,360
time flies so fast.

9
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,560
You've been gone for over 30 years.

10
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,520
I miss you.

11
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:28,720
Yongmei,

12
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:33,160
I have something

13
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,960
to tell you today.

14
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:38,040
I found a good son-in-law for our girl.

15
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,560
This young man

16
00:02:41,079 --> 00:02:42,610
has been working by my side,

17
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,260
and he's just like me when I was young.

18
00:02:54,079 --> 00:02:55,410
What are you doing here?

19
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,360
You have people following me every day,

20
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,880
stopping me from seeing him.

21
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:00,400
You don't even answer my calls.

22
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,080
What else could I do but come here?

23
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,610
It's no use chasing me here.

24
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,560
I will never agree

25
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,920
to what you're asking.

26
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,920
Let me tell you, even if

27
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,050
you won't let me see him,

28
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,680
I will never be with
that manager you set me up

29
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,560
with.

30
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,530
If the manager won't do,

31
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,560
what about the cop I introduced you to?

32
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,200
Or Uncle Wang's son?

33
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:26,760
I don't...

34
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:28,360
I don't like any of them.

35
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,520
Dad, I'm a human being.

36
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,880
I'm not a machine.

37
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:34,440
I can't be

38
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,400
with someone I don't like.

39
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:38,160
Why?

40
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:39,000
Why do you always make me

41
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,680
live according to your ideas?

42
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,040
Because I'm your dad.

43
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:45,620
Because I have over 30 years
more life experience than you.

44
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,340
I see things very clearly.

45
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,400
That artist guy you found

46
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:52,200
is just a freeloader.

47
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:53,760
You two are

48
00:03:54,079 --> 00:03:55,010
not a good match.

49
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:58,120
What do you mean by a good match?

50
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,760
He's young now

51
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,860
and hasn't achieved much yet.

52
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,130
But weren't you young once?

53
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,720
When my mom got together with you,

54
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:09,880
weren't you penniless with nothing?

55
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:12,200
My grandparents opposed it so strongly.

56
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,240
It was my mom.

57
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,400
If my mom hadn't

58
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,000
risked everything to be with you,

59
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,800
would you be where you are today?

60
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,360
Now that you have money,

61
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,600
you look down on young people

62
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:23,960
who are struggling just like you did.

63
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,660
Do you think this is
what my mom would want to see?

64
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:31,120
You're forgetting your roots.

65
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,640
It's a betrayal.

66
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,800
You not only betrayed yourself,

67
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,400
but you also betrayed my mom.

68
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,040
Nonsense!

69
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,480
I'm doing this for your own good.

70
00:04:54,159 --> 00:04:55,159
For me?

71
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,000
You've always

72
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,600
only cared about yourself.

73
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,300
If only you were still here...

74
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:14,300
How nice that would be.

75
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:23,960
Here's the thing.

76
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,760
We've set up a special task force.

77
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,880
Given your father's special status

78
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:30,280
and the significant attention
this has drawn,

79
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,960
we will definitely find out the truth

80
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,320
and reconstruct what really happened.

81
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,120
Rest assured.

82
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:36,760
Also, as his only family member,

83
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:39,000
please let us know
if you have any requests.

84
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,800
We'll do our best to accommodate them.

85
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,260
I don't have any requests.

86
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:44,240
Just handle it as soon as possible,

87
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,760
so my father can be cremated

88
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:46,690
and laid to rest.

89
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,800
May I ask

90
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,400
how your relationship with your father is?

91
00:05:53,159 --> 00:05:54,320
Well,

92
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:56,520
before you two arrived,

93
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:58,200
I had a chat with Ms. Gao.

94
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:58,440
Ms. Gao

95
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,360
even asked me

96
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:00,720
how my relationship with my parents is,

97
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:01,240
right?

98
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,760
Are you trying to ask

99
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,720
why I don't look sad?

100
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:17,660
Officer Jiang, you must have
a great relationship with your parents.

101
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,400
It's okay.

102
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,960
My mom loves to nag.

103
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,160
My dad is a college professor,

104
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:21,960
the old-school type.

105
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:23,160
He doesn't talk much.

106
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,040
I can tell.

107
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,840
They must love you very much.

108
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:30,000
Are you saying

109
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:31,840
your father

110
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,360
doesn't love you?

111
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:39,360
I guess he does.

112
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,800
Officer Weng,

113
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,840
are you suspecting me

114
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,480
by asking that?

115
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,280
You're overthinking it.

116
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:52,880
It's just a routine inquiry.

117
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,320
Shen Xi,

118
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:59,080
the perpetrator.

119
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:00,560
Do you know her?

120
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:08,160
Shen Xi, what is your profession?

121
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:11,760
A dance teacher.

122
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:14,920
At Star Art School

123
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,050
right here in Checheng.

124
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,600
Did you major in dance in college?

125
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,800
I majored in acting,

126
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,440
but

127
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,720
I've been learning dance
since I was a kid.

128
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,200
Then why didn't you go to Beijing

129
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,660
or Hengdian to be an actor,

130
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,650
but came back to our small city?

131
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:37,690
I drifted in Beijing for five years

132
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:40,020
and couldn't hold on anymore.

133
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,760
My parents insisted I come back,

134
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,960
so I did.

135
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:47,440
Do you live with your parents?

136
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,120
I live on my own.

137
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,840
Because I got used to

138
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:55,960
living alone in Beijing,

139
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,880
living with my parents

140
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,600
actually feels a bit inconvenient.

141
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,080
I rented a place near the school.

142
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,400
What do your parents do?

143
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,000
Teachers.

144
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,220
Primary school teachers.

145
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,080
But they're both retired now.

146
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:17,880
Do you know Gao Yuhai,

147
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:19,740
the one who was hit?

148
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:23,000
Yes.

149
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,520
You do?

150
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,850
What's your relationship?

151
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,600
No,

152
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,000
you misunderstood.

153
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,559
When I said I know him,

154
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:35,120
I meant he's a celebrity
in our Motor City.

155
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:37,780
I've seen him
in many newspapers and magazines.

156
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:41,020
I really didn't recognize him

157
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,080
last night.

158
00:08:44,159 --> 00:08:45,440
Maybe it's because

159
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,730
I was too scared at the time.

160
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,160
We will continue

161
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:52,890
to investigate this accident.

162
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,600
Please don't leave

163
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,600
Motor City for a while.

164
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,520
We need your cooperation.

165
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:00,040
Also, we need to impound your car

166
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,400
for a period of time.

167
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:08,320
Captain Weng, what do you think?

168
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,120
Shen Xi,

169
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:13,800
judging from her words,

170
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,360
micro-expressions, and reactions,

171
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,880
she has no problem at all.

172
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,090
Let's wait for Jiang

173
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,560
and see what he finds.

174
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,160
Shen Xi and Gao Yuhai

175
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:25,600
are indeed from two different worlds.

176
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:27,600
Their lives don't intersect at all.

177
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:31,160
Unless she lied to us.

178
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,880
Captain Li, Wei,

179
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:35,480
I've finished the basic background check

180
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,200
on Shen Xi.

181
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,080
Take a look.

182
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,520
I also put together a timeline

183
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:45,160
of her and Gao Yuhai.

184
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:47,440
Let's go back to the office
and check it out.

185
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:47,920
Okay.

186
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,320
After graduating from college,
Shen Xi stayed in Beijing

187
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,780
and worked for five years,

188
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:56,680
mainly acting.

189
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:58,400
She returned to Checheng two years ago

190
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:00,960
and worked as a dance teacher
at a dance school.

191
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:03,280
This school mainly has
two types of students:

192
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,600
kids taking grading tests

193
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:06,920
or hobby classes,

194
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,080
and art exam candidates.

195
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,560
I asked her colleagues.

196
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:12,960
Their impression of her is
that she's serious,

197
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,360
quiet, and highly professional.

198
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,280
But she usually keeps to herself

199
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:18,280
and doesn't have many close friends

200
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:19,160
or besties.

201
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,720
If there has to be one,

202
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,640
it's Shen Xi.

203
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:39,000
She participated in a competition

204
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:39,960
called the Peach Blossom Cup a year ago.

205
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:40,920
And this competition

206
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:43,560
happened to be title-sponsored
by Wending Group.

207
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:44,760
Then Shen Xi lied.

208
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:46,200
She does know Gao Yuhai.

209
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,600
She really doesn't know him.

210
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,680
Because Wending Group sponsors

211
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:52,400
dozens of such events a year.

212
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:55,400
The chairman, Gao Yuhai,
rarely attends them.

213
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:56,120
Jiang,

214
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,960
go find the person in charge
of that competition.

215
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,120
We still need to ask.

216
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:02,280
Don't miss any useful information.

217
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:04,040
Gao Yuhai goes back
to his old house every Saturday.

218
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:05,760
This is the only way.

219
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:08,560
But everyone knows this information.

220
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,160
Captain Li,

221
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:13,000
what's there to re-examine?

222
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,680
Except for that white screen window,

223
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:16,280
there's nothing else.

224
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,520
Captain Li,

225
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,680
thank you for bringing me
into the task force.

226
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:27,410
I will definitely work harder.

227
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:33,860
Captain Li,

228
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:37,080
Wei looks a bit serious.

229
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:38,960
Are all female detectives like this?

230
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:39,680
Unlike you,

231
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,720
who looks so amiable.

232
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,930
I used to be a detective too.

233
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:47,240
Detectives

234
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,900
deal with criminal cases.

235
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:52,560
And they have to deal with
all kinds of suspects.

236
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,160
How can they solve cases
if they are gentle,

237
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:54,600
right?

238
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:56,120
Then why did you transfer

239
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,880
from the criminal investigation team
to the traffic police?

240
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,280
Being a detective is so great.

241
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,880
You get to handle major cases.

242
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:01,680
Life-and-death situations,

243
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:02,240
Sherlock Holmes,

244
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:02,840
Keigo Higashino...

245
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,040
Are you a chatterbox?

246
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:04,800
Did you find out about

247
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:05,840
the person in charge
of the dance competition

248
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:06,970
I asked you to check?

249
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:09,760
No.

250
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,400
Since you didn't check that,

251
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,960
did you look into Gao Yuhai's background?

252
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,160
I did check that.

253
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,080
Gao Yuhai comes
from an ordinary background.

254
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:19,410
But his father-in-law is quite a big shot.

255
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:21,600
His father-in-law?

256
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:23,400
You mean

257
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:26,280
he made his fortune relying
on his father-in-law?

258
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,240
You're smart as always, Captain Li.

259
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,760
How does the saying go...

260
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,800
Marrying well is better
than working hard 045509.

261
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:54,300
Captain Li, I'm done writing.

262
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,800
Yan Yongmei is Gao Yuhai's late wife.

263
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,200
When they first got married,

264
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:00,720
they squeezed into a small courtyard

265
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,040
in the mountains
behind the thermal power plant.

266
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,200
Yan Yongmei died of a severe hemorrhage

267
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:04,760
during a difficult labor
with their daughter,

268
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,200
Gao Yayan.

269
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:08,200
He never remarried after that.

270
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:10,400
In many of his personal interviews,

271
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,400
Gao Yuhai has said

272
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:12,280
that he wouldn't be where he is today

273
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:13,440
without his wife.

274
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,880
She was his lucky star

275
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,960
and the only wife he would ever have.

276
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:19,000
Since her passing,

277
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,600
Gao Yuhai would spend every Saturday night

278
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:22,720
at the old house where her ashes are kept,

279
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:23,480
to mourn

280
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:24,680
her.

281
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:25,600
This accident

282
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,040
happened on his way to the old house,

283
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:29,300
where he was struck and killed by Shen Xi.

284
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,440
Has that tricycle been brought
back to the station?

285
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,160
Not yet.

286
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:37,360
I just asked the local police station.

287
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:40,220
They'll send it over
first thing tomorrow morning.

288
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:01,440
Xingchen, you're not asleep, right?

289
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,360
Mom's here.

290
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,320
What is it, Mom?

291
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:05,680
Why are you drinking ice water again?

292
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:07,120
Didn't I tell you not to?

293
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,440
It's bad for your stomach.

294
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,040
Mom, I'm over 30.

295
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,480
Can you leave me alone about this?

296
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,000
Give it to me.

297
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,560
Drink this. I just warmed it up.

298
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:15,040
You know you're 30,

299
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:18,040
so why don't you bring a girl home?

300
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:19,160
Listen,

301
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:20,520
Zheng from the station,

302
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:21,360
his wife

303
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:22,880
found you another match. Mom...

304
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:23,960
I need to take a shower.

305
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:24,600
I have a case tomorrow.

306
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:25,640
Don't push me.

307
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:27,080
You're pushing me again.

308
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:27,720
You won't meet her?

309
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:28,640
Good night.

310
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:30,200
Good night, Mom.

311
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,960
You have milk on your mouth.

312
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:33,400
Go to bed early.

313
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:34,120
Got it.

314
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,720
How have you been lately?

315
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:52,160
Are you still in Beijing?

316
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:38,480
Captain Li,

317
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,840
This car is pretty old.

318
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:49,040
It's the earliest model
from the Dongfeng factory, right?

319
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,080
But then again,

320
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,880
anyone who owned a car like this back then

321
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,360
was no ordinary person.

322
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,480
But then again,

323
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:58,720
here in Checheng,

324
00:16:58,720 --> 00:16:59,800
electric bikes,

325
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:03,200
tricycles, auto-rickshaws, and motorcycles

326
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,329
are everywhere now.

327
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,480
Is there a problem?

328
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,520
On the night of the incident,

329
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:11,680
this vehicle was parked by the road.

330
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:13,240
The path was narrow,

331
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:15,560
blocking Gao Yuhai's way.

332
00:17:16,359 --> 00:17:19,240
Then Gao Yuhai walked around it

333
00:17:21,079 --> 00:17:23,339
and stepped into the motor vehicle lane,

334
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,970
which caused the accident.

335
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,880
That's the situation, Captain Li.

336
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,000
But I still think

337
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:32,160
it's quite common for tricycles
like this to be parked by the road.

338
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,240
In just the few months
I've been working here,

339
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:35,480
I've lost count of how many I've cleared.

340
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:37,540
This really doesn't prove anything.

341
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:41,090
We still can't leave anything out.

